[{"id":4892634619,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI5-t-w","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"c8ad4e85465a141052226bd7a202ec31bb9f7ce5","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?u=380bea11a30c8cb9a25651d120a4a85904ced8e3&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","login":"rburing","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing"},"body":"I agree the most practical way to add these kinds of methods to Godot 4.x is to add them with a suffix in the name. However, I think `_typed`, while shorter, is not as informative as the `_no_alloc` from the original proposal. In my opinion the zero allocation part of the API is important to highlight, more so than the new API being more typed. Also, the \"typedness\" is already present in the function signature, so it is redundant to mention it again in the function name. When adding this new feature, we also have the opportunity to teach users something, and I think we should better use it to teach about zero allocation APIs than about typing.\n\nI agree with storing the maximum number of results on the result object (for the user to pre-fill), since that is where the allocation happens. Letting this number be arbitrary (non-negative) allows to make it zero, which could be a convenient way to \"disable\" a query. There is a question of what the setter of this property should do when the object already contains results, more than the new size would allow for. In my opinion it should also set the *number of results* to the minimum of the previous number of results and the new size, to avoid putting the object in an \"invalid state\", and keeping typical loops over results valid. (It's an edge case, but still we should handle it the best we can.)\n\nWith the new result objects we do have the opportunity to choose the naming around the list of results, for those methods that return multiple results. In particular there is the name of the class, and we have the names of the properties and (index) parameters that refer to an individual result. I'm not a fan of the \"collision\" naming (`max_collisions`, `collision_count`, `collision_index`) for individual results because it does not make a lot of sense for a point intersection query, and I would prefer a uniform naming scheme (predictable for users). I agree with @Chestnut45's suggestion to go with a generic \"result\" naming (`max_results`, `result_count`, `result_index`) for the properties and parameters that refer to individual results, also matching the naming in the internal physics API. In the cases where this applies, I think the name \"...Result2D\" or \"...Result3D\" for the class is suboptimal, because it suggests putting it in a variable named `result`, which then makes it awkward to have a loop over `result.result_count`. So I would suggest \"...Results2D\" and \"...Results3D\" in these cases.\n\nI'm less sure about the following (feel free to discuss), but instead of a (read-only) `result_count` property, one could also have a `count()` method, and instead of a `max_results` property one could have a `resize(max_results: int)` setter method (and perhaps a `size()` getter method). (Another option is to use `size()` instead of `result_count`, but then naming the method(s) to replace `max_results` becomes difficult.)\n\nThis might also need a GDScript team or core team review to evaluate if adding (many) read-only properties like in this PR is acceptable. I've proposed this pattern in the past and was told to use getters instead, since read-only properties can be an unexpected behavior for GDScript users.\n\nOne could also argue for allowing multiple results from ray queries, or question the need for having three different shape query methods, but I'm not sure if it would take a lot of time to implement and unify those (comments welcome).\n\nP.S. Instead of `[code skip-lint]result[/code]` it should be `[param result]`, a few times.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4892634619","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-09T21:38:16Z"},{"id":4964729066,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ-vA6g","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"6930da068b37583e2ded98d93e34e6c9bcd260f6","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?u=380bea11a30c8cb9a25651d120a4a85904ced8e3&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","login":"rburing","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing"},"body":"This looks almost ready to me now. See my new comments on the documentation.\r\n\r\nThe read-only properties were kept in the latest push. I [inquired](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/gdscript?msg=cyPRutgC0lO0Q07bw) about this on RocketChat in the `#gdscript` channel, and did not really find strong opposition to them, so I am fine with keeping them.\r\n\r\nSomeone brought up that the `_no_alloc` methods could still heap allocate internally, and probably do in some cases. In my opinion the (lack of) allocation for the return value is the more important one (e.g. for C#, if I understand correctly), and so in my current interpretation that's what the suffix refers to, and I still like the name. I think in theory we can also make the methods always non-allocating internally in the future, by exposing some way to (optionally) pre-allocate the necessary internal buffers (per thread?). It could be argued that that should be done before merging this PR, but personally I do not mind leaving it as a follow-up.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4964729066","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-18T20:21:09Z"},{"id":4965988918,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ_76Ng","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"26643c46eb58d95f3a2f5c02ff2954083c32c3bf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?u=380bea11a30c8cb9a25651d120a4a85904ced8e3&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","login":"rburing","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4965988918","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-18T21:37:07Z"},{"id":4966678936,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKAmBmA","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"26643c46eb58d95f3a2f5c02ff2954083c32c3bf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?u=380bea11a30c8cb9a25651d120a4a85904ced8e3&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","login":"rburing","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4966678936","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-18T22:51:42Z"},{"id":4969022693,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKC1E5Q","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"26643c46eb58d95f3a2f5c02ff2954083c32c3bf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47152052?u=7f3c243e5d49c4a158e099edfb548e77102dfea1&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/aterray","id":47152052,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTUyMDUy","login":"aterray","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/aterray"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4969022693","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-08-19T06:19:14Z"},{"id":4970993093,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKEtVxQ","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"26643c46eb58d95f3a2f5c02ff2954083c32c3bf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?u=380bea11a30c8cb9a25651d120a4a85904ced8e3&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","login":"rburing","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4970993093","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-19T10:13:06Z"},{"id":4971004581,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKEuCpQ","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"26643c46eb58d95f3a2f5c02ff2954083c32c3bf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?u=380bea11a30c8cb9a25651d120a4a85904ced8e3&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","login":"rburing","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4971004581","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-19T10:14:24Z"},{"id":4762563576,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG97z-A","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"26643c46eb58d95f3a2f5c02ff2954083c32c3bf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","login":"AThousandShips","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4762563576","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-20T10:07:45Z"},{"id":4976988954,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKKbTGg","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"20b3c5dcc40305194ab7652de6653600912dfac7","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","login":"mihe","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe"},"body":"I've personally had three main gripes with this PR (and others like it):\r\n\r\n1. Passing in an object to be written into is a bit unorthodox for the Godot API in general, and could be confusing. However, it seems there's precedence for this with `NavigationServer*D.query_path` already, so that arguably makes that point moot. (**EDIT:** I totally forgot about `PhysicsServer*D.body_test_motion` as well, which was obviously mentioned in the PR description)\r\n2. I didn't like the `_typed` suffix, and I frankly don't like the new `_no_alloc` suffix either, but more on that below.\r\n3. Having both variants sit alongside eachother, potentially confusing people. Granted, the query API isn't very approachable to begin with, but that also isn't an argument for making it more confusing.\r\n\r\nWith that said, I agree that this approach is probably the more pragmatic way of achieving this in any kind of near future.\r\n\r\nGiven the size of this PR, and what little time I have available, I've limited my review to only the 3D side of it for now, since that's the side I have most experience with. A lot of my comments likely translate directly to the 2D side of things, so feel free to apply my feedback there as well. I might do another pass to cover the 2D side at a later point.\r\n\r\nI've left a number of duplicate comments, for issues found in multiple files, but in the interest of keeping the number of comments down I also left a few file-wide comments where the issues across the files are largely the same. If you'd prefer I just make individual comments that you can easily resolve one-by-one, I'm happy to do so.\r\n\r\nIf some of my comments conflict with previous feedback, make it known before changing anything.\r\n\r\nOne common thread across the PR seems to be that there's some divergence between the new documentation and the old documentation, which I think is unfortunate. I would say let's keep them in sync as best we can, either by having the new documentation just copy the old, or by workshopping new descriptions for both in this PR, but the latter might increase the scope of this PR too much.\r\n\r\nAs for the naming scheme, I'm personally not a fan of `_no_alloc`. The no allocation \"promise\" isn't true today, and it might not be true for a while, possibly never. I'm all for pursuing less heap allocations, but promising exactly zero forever is not something we have the ability to enforce right now, and I think any amount of heap allocations in a `_no_alloc` function is highly misleading.\r\n\r\nAlternative suggestions for suffixes, in order of personal preference:\r\n\r\n1. `_into`, e.g. `intersect_ray_into`, as in you're writing the results into the provided argument. `_to` could be another alternative to this.\r\n    - I prefer this one myself, but I'll admit that `_into` is maybe somewhat ambiguous, since we're talking about spatial queries.\r\n2. `_buffer`, e.g. `intersect_ray_buffer`, as in you're writing into a pre-allocated buffer, as opposed to allocating something new.\r\n   - Buffer typically refers to a raw chunk of memory in my experience, not so much a class object, but I'd say this one at least captures the allocation scheme better than `_into`, without promising zero allocations.\r\n3. `_in_place`, e.g. `intersect_ray_in_place`, as in you're writing the results in-place, as opposed to allocating something new.\r\n    - Similar to `_into` in that it might be ambiguous in the context of spatial queries.\r\n4. `_result`, e.g. `intersect_ray_result`, as in you're writing into a result object.\r\n    - Maybe a bit confusing at first glance.\r\n6. Version number, e.g. `intersect_ray2`. This has plenty of precedence in the GDExtension API, but I don't believe there's any in the scripting API.\r\n    - Straight-forward, but not particularly attractive, in my opinion.\r\n\r\nI'd be curious to hear what others think about them.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4976988954","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-08-20T12:11:37Z"},{"id":4984063411,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKRLFsw","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"26643c46eb58d95f3a2f5c02ff2954083c32c3bf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47152052?u=7f3c243e5d49c4a158e099edfb548e77102dfea1&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/aterray","id":47152052,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTUyMDUy","login":"aterray","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/aterray"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-4984063411","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-08-20T14:51:52Z"},{"id":4984310673,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKRaLkQ","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"26643c46eb58d95f3a2f5c02ff2954083c32c3bf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48457382?u=317013c8112a59cae43303402a913bd3e776128d&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Chestnut45","id":48457382,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NDU3Mzgy","login":"Chestnut45","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godot