","login":"mihe","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-5007087096","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-08-24T11:00:07Z"},{"id":5121816010,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMUi1yg","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"2a5bffc86a51b8e2700593ff3364ccd864aff4f9","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","login":"mihe","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe"},"body":"Alright, mostly just a couple of minor things left to address, as seen in the new comments, so as far as I'm concerned the 3D side of this looks fine overall now. I haven't looked at the 2D side at all myself, and probably won't have time to, but I trust that it mirrors the 3D side of things.\r\n\r\nAfter some internal discussions we decided to take this chance to deprecate the `collider` field on the internal `RayResult` and `ShapeResult` objects (see #122745) in order to get rid of the fairly detrimental `ObjectDB::get_instance` call that's currently forced upon the physics servers, and instead move it to happen at each individual call site for Godot's internal usage of it.\r\n\r\nWe'll still be populating the `\"collider\"` field in the `Dictionary`-returning versions of the physics queries, for compatibility reasons, but given how easy it is to do `instance_from_id` from scripts using the `collider_id` field, it seems harmless to remove those getters/properties entirely from the result objects here, like `PhysicsIntersectPointResult*D`.\r\n\r\nSo if/when #122745 is merged, we can remove `collider`/`get_collider` from the result objects here. No need to do it before then.\r\n\r\nEDIT: Alternatively we leave the `get_collider` getters there and have them do the `ObjectDB::get_instance` call, like `KinematicCollision*D`. I have no strong feelings one way or the other.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs for the topic of the suffix:\r\n\r\n- Thinking about `_in_place`/`_inplace` some more, especially given how C++ uses it, might in fact make it less fitting, since it's more about placement construction given some set of parameters, rather than filling an out-parameter, but maybe I'm nitpicking.\r\n- `_buffered` to me is something very different from `_buffer`, making me think of buffered input or I/O in general, as in you're storing a series of something for some kind of deferral.\r\n- `_into` has some precedence in popular languages/APIs as well, with largely the exact same purpose as what we're doing here, like Python's [`socket.recv_into`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/socket.html#socket.socket.recv_into), Kotlin's [`*Array.copyInto`](https://kotlinlang.org/api/core/kotlin-stdlib/kotlin.collections/copy-into.html), the web's [`TextEncoder.encodeInto`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/TextEncoder/encodeInto), and I'm sure many more. But again, the spatial ambiguity is not ideal.\r\n\r\nMy vote is still on `_into`, but I'd like to see some other maintainers sign off on it as well.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970#pullrequestreview-5121816010","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113970","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-09-05T21:42:42Z"},{"id":5124687246,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMXSFjg","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"2a5bffc86a51b8e2700593ff3364ccd864aff4f9","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_ur